This practical focused on protein sequence comparison through online BLAST and a Python-based non-gapped global alignment with BLOSUM62. The human DLX5 protein is 289 amino acids in length and localised to the nucleus.

BLAST analysis returned 250 hits, with sequence identities ranging from 52.3% to 100%. The identity between human and mouse DLX5 was measured at 96.5%.

Three pairwise alignments were processed in Python. Human and mouse DLX5 yielded a high BLOSUM62 score and 96.5% identity. Alignments involving a random sequence produced low scores and near-random identity values.

These results confirm human and mouse DLX5 are the most closely related, demonstrating clear evolutionary conservation and biological homology.